I have all the findings. Here is my report.

## Summary

The "registration date" business-day rule lives in the spring-petclinic-style codebase under the `rest.function.owner` package. Notably, the **production code only rolls weekends forward, while the tests/spec expect it to also skip public holidays** — production has no holiday logic at all.

## 1. Business-day adjustment (production code)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RegistrationDate.java`** — the core rule. Package-private helper class:

```java
static LocalDate effective(LocalDate supplied) {
    return toBusinessDay(supplied != null ? supplied : LocalDate.now());
}

/** Roll a weekend date forward to the following Monday; a weekday is returned unchanged. */
static LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate date) {
    while (date.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY || date.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY) {
        date = date.plusDays(1);
    }
    return date;
}
```

Note: this only skips Saturday/Sunday. There is **no holiday handling** here.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ApplyRegistrationDate.java`** — the OfficeFloor function that applies the rule to the owner being built:

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    owner.setRegistrationDate(RegistrationDate.effective(owner.getRegistrationDate()));
}
```

Two other production classes consume the same rule:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RequireDailyCapacity.java`** — caps owners per adjusted business day (uses `RegistrationDate.effective(...)`, `DAILY_LIMIT = 100`, throws `DailyLimitExceededException`).

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RequireCurrentRegistrationDate.java`** — validates the *raw* supplied date is not in the future (throws `FutureRegistrationDateException`); runs before any business-day adjustment. Does not itself adjust dates.

Related escalation/exception classes:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyLimitExceededException.java`

## 2. Tests for the registration-date / business-day logic

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — the only direct test. Its class-level comment states the intended rule ("the default registration date rolls past **public holidays as well as weekends**"), but the black-box assertion only checks the weekend invariant:

```java
@Test
void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
    DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(
            fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(structuredOwner())).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
    assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
}
```

## 3. Public holiday logic

The only holiday logic in the repository is **test-side reference data**, in the base class:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** (lines ~239-274):

```java
/** Fixed public holidays the business-day roll skips (year of the run). */
protected static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
        LocalDate.parse("2026-01-01"), LocalDate.parse("2026-01-26"),
        LocalDate.parse("2026-04-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-28"));

/** Roll a date forward over weekends and pinned holidays to the next business day. */
protected LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate d) {
    while (d.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY || d.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY
            || HOLIDAYS.contains(d)) {
        d = d.plusDays(1);
    }
    return d;
}
```

## Key discrepancy

The test harness's `toBusinessDay` (AcceptanceBase) and the spec comments (AcceptanceTest, and the "public holidays as well as weekends" wording) expect the roll to skip **both weekends and public holidays**. The production implementation (`RegistrationDate.toBusinessDay`) skips **only weekends** and contains no `HOLIDAYS` set or equivalent. There is no production-side public-holiday calendar anywhere under `src/main`.

